-- ============================================================================
-- OceanBase Database 4.4.2 — SELECT Composition, Function, Hint & Conversion Catalog
-- Generated: 2026-11-14T05:08:29+00:00
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc
-- Source revision: V4.4.2 branch, commit 017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878
--
-- PURPOSE
-- A source-linked reference of documented SELECT forms and representative compositions.
-- It preserves every SQL function-documentation page and every documented SQL syntax
-- block in the OceanBase 4.4.2 MySQL-mode and Oracle-mode function directories.
--
-- IMPORTANT — THE MEANING OF "ALL COMBINATIONS"
-- SELECT expressions, subqueries, functions, windows, CTEs, set operations, and hints
-- compose recursively. Therefore the number of legal combinations is unbounded and no
-- finite SQL file can enumerate every combination. This catalog instead provides:
--   1. Every source page in the defined SELECT/function/hint/conversion inventory.
--   2. Every documented SQL syntax/argument block on those pages.
--   3. Official SELECT examples where present.
--   4. More than one hundred individually explained curated combinations.
--   5. Composition rules for generating further valid combinations.
-- This is a finite, auditable coverage contract, not a claim to enumerate infinity.
--
-- HOW TO USE
-- • Do not execute this entire file as one script. Select one example at a time.
-- • Syntax diagrams are commented out; replace placeholders with real SQL tokens.
-- • Active examples may require tables, indexes, partitions, external locations,
--   privileges, transactions, sample data, or optional OceanBase features.
-- • Examples are source-derived/curated and statically checked, not executed against
--   a live OceanBase 4.4.2 server in this production environment.
-- • Check your exact 4.4.2 BP level, tenant mode, variables, licenses/edition, and EXPLAIN.
-- • Hints influence plans, not query semantics. Invalid/conflicting hints can be ignored.
-- • SELECT INTO OUTFILE writes files. Locking SELECTs affect transactional concurrency.
--
-- SAMPLE OBJECT NAMES USED BY CURATED EXAMPLES
-- employees(employee_id, department_id, manager_id, last_name, salary, hire_date,
--           profile_json, salary_text)
-- departments(department_id, department_name, active)
-- archived_employees(employee_id, department_id, manager_id, last_name, salary)
-- department_managers(department_id, manager_id)
-- department_quarterly(department_id, q1, q2, q3, q4)
-- payroll_text(employee_id, department_id, salary_text)
-- events(event_time, metric_value)
-- documents(document_id, title, body)
-- document_vectors(document_id, embedding)
-- employee_xml(xml_doc)
-- Adapt identifiers, data types, indexes, partitions, paths, and values to your schema.
--
-- TABLE OF CONTENTS
-- [C01] MySQL-mode curated SELECT combinations
-- [C02] Oracle-mode curated SELECT combinations
-- [C03] Explicit/implicit datatype conversion combinations
-- [R01] MySQL SELECT statement, JOIN/WINDOW/UNION, subqueries, and SELECT INTO
-- [R02] Oracle SELECT, CTE/JOIN/APPLY, subqueries, hierarchy, and collection SELECT
-- [H01] Shared optimizer-hint guide
-- [H02] Complete SQL-reference hint pages and argument forms
-- [T01] MySQL expression-evaluation and JSON conversion rules
-- [T02] Oracle datatype-comparison and conversion rules
-- [E01] MySQL operators and expressions usable in SELECT
-- [E02] Oracle operators, conditions, and expressions usable in SELECT
-- [F01] Complete MySQL-mode SQL function documentation inventory
-- [F02] Complete Oracle-mode SQL function documentation inventory
