-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: Overview
--   A pseudocolumn behaves like a column in a table but does not store specific values. Therefore, pseudocolumns have only read attributes and cannot be inserted, updated, or deleted. This chapter describes the pseudocolumns supported in the current version of OceanBase Database.
--   The current version of OceanBase Database supports the following pseudocolumns:
--   • Hierarchical query pseudocolumns
--   • Sequence pseudocolumns
--   • ORA_ROWSCN pseudocolumn
--   • ROWNUM pseudocolumn
--   • ROWID pseudocolumn
--   • PARTITIONID pseudocolumn
-- Documented SQL syntax: no separate SQL syntax block on this source page; see notes and source.
