-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: MAKEDATE
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   MAKEDATE() returns the date of the day number specified for dayofyear of the specified year. The value of dayofyear must be greater than 0. Otherwise, this function returns NULL.
--   If the value of dayofyear is greater than 366, the extra days more than the actual number of days of the specified year are added to the specified year. If the sum is greater than 9999, this function returns NULL.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   MAKEDATE(year,dayofyear)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT MAKEDATE(2011,31), MAKEDATE(2011,32);
-- Example 2: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT MAKEDATE(2011,0);
-- Example 3: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT MAKEDATE(2011,2917923);

