-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: TIMESTAMP
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   The first syntax returns the datetime value of the datetime expression expr.
--   The second syntax returns the datetime sum of the datetime expression expr1 and the time expression expr2. If expr2 contains date and time, only the time part is used.
--   If any argument is NULL, this function returns NULL.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   TIMESTAMP(expr)
--   TIMESTAMP(expr1,expr2)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT TIMESTAMP('2020-12-31');
-- Example 2: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT TIMESTAMP('2020-12-31 12:00:00','12:00:00');

