--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   ELT() returns a string corresponding to the specified index.
--   If N=1, the return value is str1. If N=2, the return value is str2, and so forth. If N is less than 1 or greater than the number of strings, NULL is returned.
--   The ELT() function is the complement of the FIELD() function.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   ELT(N, str1, str2, str3,...)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
