-- [F01-M0129] RPAD
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Category: SQL function reference
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/200.single-row-functions-of-mysql-mode/200.string-functions-of-mysql-mode/8100.rpad-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/200.single-row-functions-of-mysql-mode/200.string-functions-of-mysql-mode/8100.rpad-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: RPAD
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   RPAD() right-pads the str string with the padstr string to a length of len characters.
--   • If the length of str exceeds len, the leftmost len characters of str are returned.
--   • If the length of str is less than len but the length of str right-padded with padstr is greater than len, then the leftmost len characters of the string generated after padding are returned.
--   • If the length of str is less than len and the length of str right-padded with padstr is still less than len, then str is right-padded with multiple padstr strings until the length is greater than or equal to len, and the leftmost len characters of the string generated after padding are returned.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   RPAD(str,len,padstr)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT RPAD('hi',5,'?');
-- Example 2: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT RPAD('hi',1,'?');

