-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: MOD
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   MOD() returns the remainder of a number divided by another number. MOD(N,M), N % M, and N MOD M are equivalent.
--   MOD() works also for numeric values with a fractional part and returns the exact remainder after the division operation.
--   If either of N or M is NULL, the return value is NULL. If M is 0, the return value is also NULL.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   MOD(N,M)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT MOD(29,19), 29 MOD 19, 29 % 19;

