-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT() returns the approximate number of deduplicated rows for the expr expression. Only one value is returned. This function can be used to calculate the alternatives of referenced columns.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT(expr)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT last_name, salary, APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT(salary) OVER (ORDER BY hiredate) "Variance" FROM employees WHERE manager_id = 100 ORDER BY last_name, salary, "Variance";

