-- [F01-M0209] SUM
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Category: SQL function reference
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/300.aggregate-function-of-mysql-mode/1500.sum-agg-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/300.aggregate-function-of-mysql-mode/1500.sum-agg-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: SUM
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   SUM() returns the sum of expr. If the returned set does not contain any rows, NULL is returned. The DISTINCT keyword can be used to find the sum of distinct values of expr.
--   If no matching row is found, the function returns NULL.
