-- [F01-M0224] APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Category: SQL function reference
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/400.analysis-functions-of-mysql-mode/100.approx-count_distinct-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/400.analysis-functions-of-mysql-mode/100.approx-count_distinct-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT() returns the approximate number of deduplicated rows for the expr expression. Only one value is returned. The function processes a large amount of data at a much faster speed than COUNT(), and the deviation from the exact result is negligible.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT(expr) OVER over_clause
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT last_name, salary, APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT(salary) OVER (ORDER BY hiredate) "Variance"
FROM employees WHERE manager_id = 100 ORDER BY last_name, salary, "Variance";

