-- Category: SQL function reference
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/400.analysis-functions-of-mysql-mode/1400.cume-dist-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/400.analysis-functions-of-mysql-mode/1400.cume-dist-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: CUME_DIST
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   This function calculates the cumulative distribution value of a row within a group (partition) and returns a value greater than 0 and less than or equal to 1. It calculates the cumulative distribution value of a row by dividing the number of rows that are less than or equal to the current row after sorting by the total number of rows in the partition.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   CUME_DIST() OVER ([query_partition_clause] order_by_clause)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT last_name, CUME_DIST() OVER(PARTITION BY job_id ORDER BY salary) CUME_DIST FROM employees;

-- [F01-M0227] DENSE_RANK
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Category: SQL function reference
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/400.analysis-functions-of-mysql-mode/1500.dense-rank-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/400.analysis-functions-of-mysql-mode/1500.dense-rank-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: DENSE_RANK
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   DENSE_RANK() returns the rank of a data row in the column that is specified in order_by_clause.
--   Ranks are consecutive integers. Rows with the same rank value have the same rank.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   DENSE_RANK() OVER([ query_partition_clause ] order_by_clause)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT last_name, RANK() OVER(PARTITION BY job_id ORDER BY salary) rank, DENSE_RANK() OVER(PARTITION BY job_id ORDER BY salary) dense_rank, PERCENT_RANK() OVER(PARTITION BY job_id ORDER BY salary) percent_rank FROM employees;

