-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/400.analysis-functions-of-mysql-mode/1600.first_value-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: FIRST_VALUE
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   FIRST_VALUE() returns the first value of the expr expression.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   FIRST_VALUE { (expr) [ {RESPECT | IGNORE} NULLS ] | (expr [ {RESPECT | IGNORE} NULLS ])} OVER (analytic_clause)
