-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: AVG
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   AVG() returns the average value of a specified group. NULLs are ignored. The DISTINCT option can be used to return the average of distinct values of expr. If no matching row is found, AVG() returns NULL.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   AVG([ DISTINCT | ALL ] expr) OVER(analytic_clause)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
