-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/200.common-tenant-of-mysql-mode/400.functions-of-mysql-mode/400.analysis-functions-of-mysql-mode/3300.ntile-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: NTILE
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   NTILE() divides sorted rows of a partition into a specified number of groups that have the same size and returns the group number to each row. If expr is NULL, NULL is returned.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   NTILE(expr) OVER ([ query_partition_clause ] order_by_clause)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT last_name, NTILE(10) OVER(PARTITION BY job_id ORDER BY salary) ntl FROM employees;

