-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: JSON_UNQUOTE
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   JSON_UNQUOTE() unquotes a JSON value and returns the result in a utf8mb4 string.
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Description
--   json_val specifies the quoted JSON value. If the argument is NULL, NULL is returned.
--   If the value starts and ends with double quotation marks ('') but is not a valid JSON string literal, an error occurs.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   JSON_UNQUOTE(json_val)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT @jn, JSON_UNQUOTE(@jn);

