-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: ASIN
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   ASIN() returns the arc sine of a number. The arc sine is an angle whose sine is a number. The returned angle is given in radians, in the range of \[-π/2, π/2\].
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Parameters
--   number falls in the range of \[-1, 1\], and is of a numeric data type or any data type that can be implicitly converted to a numeric data type.
--   SECTION: Return type
--   The return type is NUMBER.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   ASIN(number)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT ASIN(0.5) FROM DUAL;

-- [F02-O0018] SIGN
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Category: SQL function reference
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/300.common-tenant-of-oracle-mode/500.functions-of-oracle-mode/200.single-row-functions-of-oracle-mode/100.numeric-functions-of-oracle-mode/3000.sign-of-oracle-mode.md
