-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: EMPTY_BLOB
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   EMPTY_BLOB() returns an empty BLOB locator. The locator is not NULL, and the LOB length is 0.
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Return type
--   The return type is BLOB.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   EMPTY_BLOB()
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT CASE WHEN EMPTY_BLOB() IS NULL THEN 'NULL' ELSE 'NOT NULL' END AS blob_is_null,
          DBMS_LOB.GETLENGTH(EMPTY_BLOB()) AS blob_len
          FROM DUAL;

