-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: CONTAINS
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   This function is primarily used for string matching or full-text search within database fields.
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Parameters
--   • indexed_column: The name of the column for the full-text index.
--   • search_query: The keyword or phrase to be searched, which can be of the VARCHAR2 or CLOB type.
--   • score_label: Optional. The matching number of the returned result, in NUMBER type.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   CONTAINS(indexed_column, 'search_query' [, score_label])
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT id, c1 FROM test WHERE CONTAINS(c1, 'city') > 0;

