-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: SCORE
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   This function is mainly used for string matching or full-text retrieval in database fields.
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Parameters
--   • score_label: Optional. The matching number of the returned result, in NUMBER type.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   SCORE(score_label)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT column1, column2, ...
FROM table_name
WHERE CONTAINS(indexed_column, 'search_query'[, score_label]) > 0
