-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: TZ_OFFSET
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   TZ_OFFSET() returns the time zone offset of SESSIONTIMEZONE or DBTIMEZONE.
--   Note
--   A time zone offset is the difference (in hour and minute) from the Greenwich Mean Time (GMT).
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   SESSIONTIMEZONE | The time zone of the current session.
--   DBTIMEZONE | The database time zone.
--   SECTION: Return type
--   The return type is VARCHAR2.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   TZ_OFFSET({ SESSIONTIMEZONE | DBTIMEZONE})
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT TZ_OFFSET(SESSIONTIMEZONE),TZ_OFFSET(DBTIMEZONE) FROM DUAL;

