-- [F02-O0152] TO_YMINTERVAL
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Category: SQL function reference
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/300.common-tenant-of-oracle-mode/500.functions-of-oracle-mode/200.single-row-functions-of-oracle-mode/600.conversion-functions-of-oracle-mode/3800.to-yminterval-of-oracle-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/500.sql-reference/100.sql-syntax/300.common-tenant-of-oracle-mode/500.functions-of-oracle-mode/200.single-row-functions-of-oracle-mode/600.conversion-functions-of-oracle-mode/3800.to-yminterval-of-oracle-mode.md
-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: TO_YMINTERVAL
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   This function converts a string of CHAR, VARCHAR2, NCHAR, or NVARCHAR2 data type into an INTERVAL YEAR TO MONTH value, which can be used to add or subtract from a date or datetime value.
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   \[+\ | -\] years-months | A string of CHAR, VARCHAR2, NCHAR, or NVARCHAR2 data type that conforms to this parameter format. years indicates the number of years, which must be an integer in the range \[0,999999999\]. months indicates the number of months, which must be an integer in the range \[0,11\].
--   \[-\]P\[ years Y\]\[months M\]\[days D\]\[T\[hours H\]\[minutes M\]\[seconds\[.frac_secs\]S\]\] | A string of CHAR, VARCHAR2, NCHAR, or NVARCHAR2 data type that conforms to this parameter format. frac_secs indicates the fractional part of the seconds, which must be an integer in the range \[0,999999999\]. Note The value cannot contain spaces.
--   SECTION: Return type
--   INTERVAL YEAR TO MONTH
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   /*SQL date format*/
--   TO_YMINTERVAL([+|-] years-months)
--
--   /*ISO date format*/
--   TO_YMINTERVAL([-]P[ years Y][months M][days D][T[hours H][minutes M][seconds[.frac_secs]S]])
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT SYSDATE,SYSDATE+TO_YMINTERVAL('01-02') FROM DUAL;
-- Example 2: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT TO_YMINTERVAL('P2Y6M10DT4H30M15S') FROM dual;
-- Example 3: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT TO_YMINTERVAL('-P3Y1M5D') FROM dual;

-- [F02-O0153] CONVERT
