-- Documentation and argument notes:
--   SECTION: UNISTR
--   SECTION: Purpose
--   UNISTR() converts text literals and Unicode encodings into strings in the national character set.
--   A Unicode encoded value is in the \xxxx format, where xxxx is a hexadecimal value (UCS-2 code unit) of a character in the UTF-16-encoded format. To include a backslash (\\) in a string, add another backslash before it.
--   SECTION: Syntax
--   SECTION: Parameters
--   The string parameter is a string of any character set.
--   SECTION: Return type
--   This function returns a string.
-- Documented SQL syntax 1 (syntax diagram; substitute real identifiers and values):
--   UNISTR(string)
-- Official SELECT example(s), cleaned of client prompts and result grids:
-- Example 1: demonstrates the documented behavior above; required objects and privileges must exist.
SELECT UNISTR('A B C \FF20 \00C4 \00CA \00CD \00D5 \00D8') FROM DUAL;

